[b][size=5]Playing Games[/size][/b]
<br />
<br />Games menu can be accessed via a new play button in the bottom right corner of the Title Menu, above existing buttons (see screenshots above).
<br />
<br />The mod comes with Junimo Cart and Journey of the Prairie King pre-installed so you can play them without loading into a save.
<br />
<br />An example of a game that works with this menu is [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/videos/586]Jigsaw Puzzle[/url].
<br />
<br />
<br />[b][size=5]Making Games[/size][/b]
<br />
<br />Modders can add games to the menu by accessing the mod's API, setting custom methods for clicking and drawing, e.g.:
<br />
<br />[code]public interface IStardewGamesAPI
<br />{
<br />    public void AddGame(string name, Action&lt;Rectangle, int, int&gt; clickAction, Action&lt;SpriteBatch, Rectangle&gt; drawAction);
<br />    public void ReturnToMenu();
<br />}
<br />public void GameLoop_GameLaunched(object sender, StardewModdingAPI.Events.GameLaunchedEventArgs e)
<br />{
<br />    var sgapi = Helper.ModRegistry.GetApi&lt;IStardewGamesAPI&gt;("aedenthorn.StardewGames");
<br />    if (sgapi != null)
<br />    {
<br />        sgapi.AddGame(context.ModManifest.UniqueID, ClickAction, DrawAction);
<br />    }
<br />}
<br />private void DrawAction(SpriteBatch b, Rectangle area)
<br />{
<br />    ...
<br />}
<br />private void ClickAction(Rectangle area, int x, int y)
<br />{
<br />    ...
<br />}
<br />[/code]
<br />
<br />The API passes the rectangle bounds on the screen of the game's slot to both methods, and relative click position x and y coordinates to the click action (allowing for multiple buttons, etc.).
